# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Patient data must never reach this repository.
#
# The rules below block every common extract format outright, before the
# usual Python ignores. This is deliberate belt-and-braces: the app is
# designed to be pointed at a real clinical extract, and the failure mode
# of a public repo is unrecoverable — a force-push does not remove a blob
# from a fork, a clone, or GitHub's cache.
#
# If you ever genuinely need to commit a tabular file (a lookup table, a
# tiny fixture), add it with `git add -f path/to/file.csv` and satisfy
# yourself first that it contains no patient-level data. Do not weaken
# these patterns.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.csv
*.tsv
*.parquet
*.feather
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.xls
*.dta
*.sav
*.sas7bdat
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.h5
*.hdf5

# The generated demonstration dataset lands here on first run.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# Anything obviously local or identifiable
*extract*
*patient*
*phi*
*identifiable*
secrets.toml
.streamlit/secrets.toml
.env
.env.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version

# Testing and tooling
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
